# How much of the beam-search lookahead survives into the ranking score.
#
# Measured against outcomes, not tuned by feel. Over 365 logged move->outcome
# pairs (Debug/runs, 2026-08-20..23) the lookahead bonus averaged 17.5 of a
# ~85 total score -- a fifth of the decision -- and carried no signal:
#
#   corr(lookahead(t), points(t))            = -0.09
#   corr(lookahead(t), points(t+1))          = +0.098   (n=210, ~1.4 SE)
#   corr(lookahead(t), points(t) + points(t+1)) = -0.003
#
# It is the term that is *not* paying, and it was the dominant reason the bot
# skipped the point-maximising move: in 58 of the 90 logged deviations from
# max-instant it was the largest single justification, and in 52 of them it was
# the only one (no extra move, no mode target, no blue). Replaying those logged
# candidate sets at several weights:
#
#   w=1.00 (today) 90 deviations, ~7900 real points given up
#   w=0.50         69 deviations, ~3900
#   w=0.35         63 deviations, ~3500   <- knee; 36/397 top choices change
#   w=0.00         43 deviations, ~2600
#
# 0.35 is the knee: it keeps lookahead as a tiebreaker between otherwise equal
# moves (which is all the data supports) while removing its power to outvote
# points a move actually scores. It deliberately does *not* touch the extra-move
# setup value `_with_extra_move_chain_bonus` folds into the same field -- that
# term is separately evidenced, and only the beam component is scaled here.
LOOKAHEAD_FUTURE_WEIGHT = 0.35
